--- body ---
## Context

Once 0142 lands (modules rewritten as verbatim paragraph extractions from
`prompt_complete.txt`), the existing ablation results in
`outputs/ablation/**` are based on the previous (non-verbatim) modules and
no longer reflect the canonical deep-research prompt decomposition.

This ticket re-runs the existing ablation sweep configurations with the
new modules to produce ablation data the discussion can claim is a true
decomposition of `prompt_complete`.

## Sweeps to re-run

From `experiments/experiments.toml`:

**Phase 1 — Selection across 3 regimes** (base vs. composite):
- `sweep_ablation_p1_direct_base` / `sweep_ablation_p1_direct_composite`
- `sweep_ablation_p1_rag_base` / `sweep_ablation_p1_rag_composite`
- `sweep_ablation_p1_livesearch_base` / `sweep_ablation_p1_livesearch_composite`
- `sweep_ablation_p1_direct_base_extended` (28 census models)

**Phase 2 — RAG single-module sweeps** (one module on top of base):
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_base` / `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_composite`
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_minus_*` (7 leave-one-out)
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_plus_*` (7 add-one)
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_frontier`
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_census`

Plus the new modules from 0142 may justify additional plus/minus sweeps:
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_plus_observed_vs_projected`
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_plus_pdp_completeness`
- `sweep_ablation_p2_rag_plus_data_quality_table`

## Actions

1. Verify 0142 closed and module equivalence diff passes.
2. Move existing `outputs/ablation/**` to `outputs/ablation/_pre-0143/**`
   (preserve as historical record; do not delete).
3. Add `experiments.toml` entries for the 3 new plus-sweeps if 0142
   produced new modules.
4. Re-run all Phase 1 sweeps with new modules. Compare composite results
   directly with `prompt_complete` data on the same models — should match
   modulo MoE non-determinism.
5. Re-run all Phase 2 RAG sweeps with new modules.
6. Regenerate ablation tables and figures
   (`fig_ablation_*`, `tab_ablation_*`).
7. Update the discussion text in the report to reflect that the ablation
   now decomposes `prompt_complete` verbatim.

## Cost estimate

Phase 1 + Phase 2 RAG ablation across 3 dev models × ~22 module
configurations × repeat=3 ≈ ~200 calls. Existing budget caps in
`experiments.toml`: $5–$10 per sweep, total estimate **~$30–$50**.
Confirm before launch.

## Test

- Composite ablation (all modules ON) F1 ≈ prompt_complete sweep F1
  on the same 3 models, within MoE variance. If not, the verbatim
  extraction in 0142 is incomplete.
- Phase 2 leave-one-out / add-one results show non-zero effect for at
  least the largest modules (overview, narratives, statistics).

## Exit criteria

- All ablation sweeps re-run with verbatim modules.
- Old data preserved under `outputs/ablation/_pre-0143/`.
- New tables and figures regenerated.
- Report discussion updated to claim verbatim decomposition.
- Composite-vs-complete equivalence verified on dev tier.
